     pptthhrreeaadd__ssuussppeenndd__nnpp — suspend a thread

LLIIBBRRAARRYY
     POSIX Threads Library (libpthread, -lpthread)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ##iinncclluuddee <<pptthhrreeaadd__nnpp..hh>>

     _i_n_t
     pptthhrreeaadd__ssuussppeenndd__nnpp(_p_t_h_r_e_a_d___t _t_i_d);

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssuussppeenndd__nnpp() function, called on an active thread, causes it
     to suspend.

     It is not safe for the caller of the pptthhrreeaadd__ssuussppeenndd__nnpp() function to use
     any non-async signal safe functions, except pthread_resume_np(3), until
     suspended thread is resumed, unless measures are taken to ensure that the
     thread is suspended at a safe point.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, pptthhrreeaadd__ssuussppeenndd__nnpp() function returns 0.  Otherwise, an
     error number is returned to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssuussppeenndd__nnpp() function will fail if:

     [EDEADLK]          An attempt was made to suspend the current thread.

     [EINVAL]           The value specified by the _t_i_d argument is invalid.

     [ESRCH]            No thread could be found corresponding to the thread
                        ID specified by the _t_i_d argument.

